# Git workflow (deepwiki-md-chrome-extension)

## Branches

- **`develop`** — integration branch; all feature PRs merge here first.
- **`main`** — release/stable; updated from `develop` when appropriate (not the default PR target).
- **Feature branches** — create from latest `develop`:
  - `feat/<short-description>` — new features
  - `fix/<short-description>` — bug fixes
  - `chore/<short-description>` — tooling, docs-only, version bumps

Do not commit directly to `develop` or `main` for feature work. Use a branch and open a PR.

## Commits

- Use clear, imperative messages (e.g. `Add batch download history`, `Fix ZIP download in service worker`).
- When using Cursor Agent, prefix the subject with **`[Cursor]`** (e.g. `[Cursor] Fix batch ZIP download in service worker`).
- One logical change per commit when practical; avoid unrelated file churn.

## Versioning

- **Source of truth:** `manifest.json` → `"version"`.
- On every user-facing release (or before merging a versioned PR), update:
  1. `manifest.json` version (semver: patch for fixes, minor for features, major for breaking changes).
  2. Root **`CHANGELOG.md`** — new dated section ([Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) format).
  3. **`README.md`** footer version reference if it mentions the current version.
- Store builds: `./build-for-store.sh` reads version from `manifest.json` → `deepwiki-md-extension-v<version>.zip`.

## Pull requests

- **Target branch:** `develop` (required for this project).
- PR title: include `[Cursor]` when the work was done in Cursor.
- PR body: Summary (what/why), Test plan (checklist), link related issues if any.
- Use `gh pr create --base develop` after pushing the feature branch with `-u origin <branch>`.
- Do not force-push to `develop` or `main`.

## Before opening a PR

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout develop && git pull origin develop
git checkout <your-feature-branch>
git rebase origin/develop   # or merge, per team preference; resolve conflicts
# bump version + CHANGELOG if not done yet
git push -u origin <your-feature-branch>
gh pr create --base develop --title "[Cursor] ..." --body "..."
```

## After merge

- Delete the feature branch locally/remotely when no longer needed.
- Reload the unpacked extension in Chrome after changes that affect `manifest.json` or service worker code.
